@startuml
 title PPO neural network architecture used by the project
 left to right direction
 skinparam shadowing false
 skinparam componentStyle rectangle
 skinparam packageStyle rectangle
 skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
 skinparam ArrowColor #444444

 rectangle "Observation\n(batch, 1, 72, 131)\n128 depth-image columns + 3 velocity columns" as Obs

 package "Actor: chooses the drone action" {
   rectangle "Actor feature extractor\n(separate copy)\noutputs 96 features" as ActorFeatures
   rectangle "Policy MLP\n96 -> 128 -> 64 -> 32 -> 16\nTanh activations" as ActorMLP
   rectangle "Action head\n16 -> 3 means\n+ learned log standard deviations" as ActionHead
   rectangle "Gaussian action distribution\ntraining: sample action\nevaluation: use mean\nclip each value to [-1,1]" as ActionOutput
   ActorFeatures --> ActorMLP
   ActorMLP --> ActionHead
   ActionHead --> ActionOutput
 }

 package "Critic: estimates future return during training" {
   rectangle "Critic feature extractor\n(separate copy)\noutputs 96 features" as CriticFeatures
   rectangle "Value head\n96 -> 1\nV(observation)" as ValueHead
   CriticFeatures --> ValueHead
 }

 Obs --> ActorFeatures
 Obs --> CriticFeatures

 rectangle "Normalized action output\n[x, y, z]" as Action
 ActionOutput --> Action
 rectangle "Environment maps action to velocity\n[1.5x, 1.5y + 0.5, 1.5z] m/s" as VelocityCommand
 Action ..> VelocityCommand : environment step()

 note bottom of ActorFeatures
 Both feature-extractor copies perform the same operations:
 obs_split(combined) separates image (batch,1,72,128)
 and velocity (batch,3), read from row 0's last 3 columns.

 Image path:
 conv1: 1->16; conv + max pool + LeakyReLU
 conv2: 16->32; conv + max pool + LeakyReLU
 conv3: 32->128; conv + max pool + LeakyReLU
 spatial result: 128x1x2; flatten -> 256
 image_fc1: 256->64 -> LeakyReLU
 image_fc2: 64->48

 Velocity path: vel_fc1: 3->48
 Concatenate image 48 + velocity 48 -> 96; apply Tanh.
 The actor and critic have separate extractor parameters.
 end note

 note bottom of ValueHead
 In this project ppo_train.py sets qf=[128,64,32,16].
 Installed Stable-Baselines3 2.2.1 expects vf for PPO,
 so qf is ignored. The critic therefore has no hidden MLP
 after the 96 features; its value head produces one scalar.

 During evaluation, model.predict() uses the actor only;
 the critic is for PPO training, not the movement command.
 end note
@enduml